---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const [profile] = await getCollection('profile');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Technical Investigations — Braeden Keena"
  description="Three empirical technical investigations: longitudinal pricing observatories, municipal permit pipelines, and embedded Wi-Fi CSI link forensics."
>
  <Nav name={profile.data.name} />

  <main class="inv-page">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <header class="inv-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Technical investigations</p>
        <h1 class="inv-title">Pipelines that know when they're lying to you.</h1>
        <p class="inv-lede">
          Three deep-dive engineering investigations built around empirical verification: 
          longitudinal market observatories, multi-jurisdiction public-record qualification, and hardware RF link-state forensics.
          Each project began with a number that looked complete, and each was redesigned around the controls that proved what was actually being measured.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="doors-grid">
        <!-- Door 1: Storage Price Observatory -->
        <article class="door-card door-card--storage">
          <div class="door-card__header">
            <span class="door-card__tag">Storage Price Observatory</span>
            <span class="door-card__index">01</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="door-card__title">Both Sides of the Discount Moved</h2>
          <p class="door-card__subtitle">
            A seven-source pricing monitor covering 9,077 facilities, an August rate-hike anomaly, and a pre-registered bet on Public Storage's (PSA) Q3 earnings.
          </p>

          <div class="door-card__stats">
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">9,077</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">facilities tracked across seven collections</span>
            </div>
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">129,704</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">advertised unit/offer records daily</span>
            </div>
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">4,904 / 4,904</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">listings with simultaneous rate hikes on August 1, measured by its predecessor FindStorage</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <ul class="door-card__bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>Pre-registered Q3 prediction:</strong> Sealed before Q3 results exist, predicting deceleration in promotional discount growth and new-customer contract rates below +1.6% YoY, with Q4 rates flat or negative.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The August 1st event:</strong> 4,904 listings moved into "40% off For 4 Months" and every single one received an immediate reference-rate increase (median +$45), while a July control proved rate and promo are independently writable.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The living ledger:</strong> On September 18, the September 14 rate reset was partially walked back with 12% restored across 22,772 units (0.9800 matched-panel index), observed and logged in real time.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="door-card__footer">
            <div class="door-card__tech">Python · SQLite · Leaflet · Multi-Operator Pipeline</div>
            <a href="/storage" class="door-card__cta">
              <span>Open prediction study & live dashboard</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Door 2: KC Permits -->
        <article class="door-card door-card--permits">
          <div class="door-card__header">
            <span class="door-card__tag">Civic Records & Entity Reconciliation</span>
            <span class="door-card__index">02</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="door-card__title">The Verification Filter</h2>
          <p class="door-card__subtitle">
            Turning 57,032 civic observations across 30,587 locations into 4 verifiable commercial opportunities without hallucinatory leads or naive address matching.
          </p>

          <div class="door-card__stats">
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">57,032</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">observations across 30,587 locations in database</span>
            </div>
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">21</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">municipal & county sources mapped</span>
            </div>
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">37 → 10 → 4</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">strict pipeline reconciliation: 4 prospect, 4 review, 2 excluded</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <ul class="door-card__bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>The naive scraping myth:</strong> Building permits name general contractors rather than tenant businesses, strip-mall addresses collide across dozens of suites, and speculative permits carry no operating tenant.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Tyler EnerGov reverse engineering:</strong> Extracted undocumented multi-tenant API headers (Olathe vs Overland Park vs KCMO) and discovered Overland Park houses commercial activity in <em>Plans</em> while Olathe uses <em>Permits</em>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Silent failures caught:</strong> Detected portals enforcing silent 10,000-row query truncation caps without error responses, and engineered automated run-audit reconciliation rails.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="door-card__footer">
            <div class="door-card__tech">Python · Tyler EnerGov API · pdfplumber · SQLite</div>
            <a href="/permits" class="door-card__cta">
              <span>Read lead funnel & reconciliation audit</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Door 3: CSI: Room or Radio? -->
        <article class="door-card door-card--csi">
          <div class="door-card__header">
            <span class="door-card__tag">Embedded RF Hardware & Signal Processing</span>
            <span class="door-card__index">03</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="door-card__title">Room or Radio?</h2>
          <p class="door-card__subtitle">
            A Wi-Fi CSI system identified devices at 99.7% accuracy. Physical controls broke the device-identity claim—and revealed a physical link state instead.
          </p>

          <div class="door-card__stats">
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">69,510,186</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">clean beacon frames replayed deterministically</span>
            </div>
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">29 / 35</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">distinct ideas / rejection tests carried through 8 paired nights</span>
            </div>
            <div class="door-stat">
              <strong class="door-stat__value">0.2σ vs 19.6σ</strong>
              <span class="door-stat__label">co-located boards (0.2σ) vs same board across rooms (19.6σ)</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <ul class="door-card__bullets">
            <li>
              <strong>The seductive number:</strong> 99.7% chronological holdout accuracy identifying three ESP32 transmitters using subcarrier phase slope, originally attributed to quartz crystal frequency offsets.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The hypothesis ledger:</strong> 29 distinct ideas systematically killed across 35 rejection tests, proving what the feature wasn't before claiming what it was.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The double difference:</strong> Two receivers watching the same transmitter pair in the same instant disagreed by 6.79 standard deviations—proving the measurement is a property of the link, not the radio.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="door-card__footer">
            <div class="door-card__tech">C (ESP-IDF) · Python / NumPy · RF Signal Processing</div>
            <a href="/csi" class="door-card__cta">
              <span>Open full RF investigation</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer profile={profile} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .inv-page {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 8vw, 96px);
  }

  .inv-header {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px);
  }

  .inv-title {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .inv-lede {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .doors-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
  }

  .door-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px);
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .door-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .door-card__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .door-card__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .door-card__index {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .door-card__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .door-card__subtitle {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .door-card__stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    padding-block: 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .door-stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .door-stat__value {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .door-stat__label {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .door-card__bullets {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .door-card__bullets li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 18px;
  }

  .door-card__bullets li::before {
    content: "▪";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .door-card__bullets strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .door-card__footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  }

  .door-card__tech {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .door-card__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    transition: all 0.15s ease;
  }

  .door-card__cta:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .door-card__footer {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
</style>
